   "text": {
    "L1": "Does a heavy thing always sink, and does a light thing always float?",
    "L2": "No. A heavy log can float, while a light coin can sink.",
    "L3": "Water pushes upward on objects placed in it.",
    "L4": "A solid clay ball sinks because it pushes aside only a little water.",
    "L5": "The same clay shaped as a hollow boat pushes aside more water, so the upward push can hold it up.",
    "L6": "Shape matters too: a hollow steel ship can float, while a solid steel spoon sinks.",
    "L7": "Salty water pushes up harder than plain water, so things float more easily in it."
   },
